<h1><span data-field="title" data-format="default">window_get_borderless_fullscreen</span></h1>
<p>This function returns whether a <a href="window_enable_borderless_fullscreen.htm">borderless window</a> for fullscreen mode is enabled or not.</p>
<div data-conref="../../../../assets/snippets/Note_Windows_Only_Function.hts">
<p class="note"><span data-conref="../../../../assets/snippets/Tag_note.hts"><span class="note">NOTE</span></span> This function only works on Windows.</p>
</div>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-field="title" data-format="default">window_get_borderless_fullscreen</span>();</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Bool"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Boolean</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">var _borderless = <span data-field="title" data-format="default">window_get_borderless_fullscreen</span>();<br/>
show_debug_message($&quot;Borderless Fullscreen Enabled: {_borderless}&quot;);</p>
<p>The code above calls <span class="inline3_func"><span data-field="title" data-format="default">window_get_borderless_fullscreen</span></span> to find out if borderless fullscreen is currently enabled. It then shows a debug message.</p>
<p> </p>
